<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julio Argentino Roca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a>–<a href="/years/1914">1914</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julio Argentino Roca was an Argentine general and statesman, twice president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, from 1880 to 1886 and from 1898 to 1904. As minister of war he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert">Conquest of the Desert</a> of 1878–1879, which destroyed the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranquel">Ranquel</a> and other peoples of the pampas and opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patagonia">Patagonia</a> to settlement. His presidencies consolidated the long dominance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-autonomist-party">National Autonomist Party</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julio-argentino-roca.jpg" alt="Julio Argentino Roca" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Julio_roca_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
